# Human design principles

Applies to `cases`, `admin`, `auth`, `contractor`, `forms`, `workflow`, and
`widgets`. Emotion targets: **confident, professional, calm**.

## When changing UI

- **Destructive**: Confirm dialog before revoke / suspend / delete. Do not invent a one-off without a confirm.
- **Feedback**: Toast (Sonner) or `role="status"` / `role="alert"` for success/failure.
- **Empty**: Shared empty-state component with **one** primary CTA when a path exists.
- **Loading**: Layout-matched skeleton — never bare "Loading…".
- **Motion / touch**: Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`; no hover-only critical controls.
- **Routes**: English path segments only (see English-route-paths rule).
- **Shared UI**: Prefer `@algenium/blocks` for shared product chrome. Copy shadcn/ui primitives into the repo (`src/components/ui/*`).

## Do not

- Destructive actions without confirmation
- Bare "Loading…" when a skeleton exists for that surface
- Hover-only critical controls on touch devices
- Decorative motion that ignores reduced-motion preferences
- Empty states with no next step when one clearly exists
